#IO PNML

PNML (Petri Net Markup Language) is the standard XML exchange format for Petri
nets. This module handles both export and import.

Export serialises a GameNet to a PNML string. The standard elements carry the
net topology and layout positions. Game-specific data lives in toolspecific
elements so vanilla PNML readers ignore it cleanly.

A GameNet carries three markings, one per token colour, and the file says
each as a count on a place. The chomper marking is the net's own initial
marking: the standard initialMarking element, with playerStart naming a place
that holds the chomper when it carries no count. The ghost and dot markings
are tokens elements in the place's toolspecific block, each naming its
colour: a tokens element for ghost with the number as its text means that
many ghosts there, and a bare one means one. A place says nothing about a
colour when it has the colour's default.

The colours are declared once, in the net's toolspecific block, as a colours
element holding a colour element for each. A declaration says a colour's
default count, which is what every place with no tokens element of that
colour holds; for the chomper, that its marking is the standard
initialMarking; and whether a life lost deals it again (reset restore) or
leaves it alone (reset keep). An attribute left out means the built-in value:
the dot has a default of one and is kept on reset, the chomper and the ghost
have a default of none and are dealt again. With no declaration at all the
three built-in colours apply, so a vanilla net or a hand-written map need say
nothing.

Only the three colours the game has rules for are honoured. A declaration for
any other colour is reported and ignored, and so are tokens elements naming
one, so a file written for a later version still loads.

Version 0.8.0 and earlier used a different format, a ghostSpawn element on a
transition and a hasDot element to suppress a dot. Those are not read, so a
map written that way loads with no ghosts and a dot on every place; the
CHANGELOG records the change.

Import is split into functions that can be claimed without a browser.
resolveColours turns the declarations into the defaults and the colours kept
on reset. buildGameNet takes plain #RawPlace, #RawTrans, and #RawArc records
and assembles a GameNet: it scale-fits all positions to the 950×780 canvas,
builds the net, resolves the chomper marking (all toolspecific playerStart
elements > all initialMarking places > first place as fallback), and
collects the ghost and dot markings. importPNML is a thin browser wrapper: it
calls DOMParser to parse the XML string into a Document, extracts the raw
records, then delegates to those. importPNML itself cannot be claimed —
DOMParser is not available in the tsx runtime — so the full XML round-trip
remains documented in prose rather than the claim layer.

When loading vanilla PNML (no toolspecific extensions), the built-in
defaults apply: every place gets a dot, the first marked place holds the
chomper, and there are no ghosts.

The built-in colours, and what a declaration may change about them. A colour
element's attributes are all optional and name only what differs from the
built-in value.

    const COLOURS: ColourName[] = ['chomper', 'ghost', 'dot'];
    const DEFAULT_KEEP: ColourName[] = ['dot'];
    const BUILT_IN_DEFAULTS: Record<ColourName, number> =
      { chomper: 0, ghost: 0, dot: 1 };

    type RawColour = {
      name: string; default?: number; marking?: string; reset?: string;
    };

    interface ColourRules {
      defaults: Record<ColourName, number>;
      keepOnReset: ColourName[];
      warnings: string[];
    }

    function resolveColours(declared: RawColour[]): ColourRules {
      const defaults = { ...BUILT_IN_DEFAULTS };
      const keep = new Set<ColourName>(DEFAULT_KEEP);
      const warnings: string[] = [];

      for (const d of declared) {
        const name = COLOURS.find(c => c === d.name);
        if (!name) {
          warnings.push(`colour '${d.name}' is not one the game has rules for; ignored`);
          continue;
        }
        if (d.default !== undefined) {
          if (!Number.isInteger(d.default) || d.default < 0) {
            warnings.push(`colour '${name}': default must be a whole number, not ${d.default}`);
          } else if (name === 'chomper' && d.default !== 0) {
            warnings.push(`colour 'chomper': a default other than none is not supported; ignored`);
          } else {
            defaults[name] = d.default;
          }
        }
        if (d.marking !== undefined && !(name === 'chomper' && d.marking === 'initial')) {
          warnings.push(`colour '${name}': marking '${d.marking}' is not supported; ignored`);
        }
        if (d.reset === 'keep') keep.add(name);
        else if (d.reset === 'restore') keep.delete(name);
        else if (d.reset !== undefined) {
          warnings.push(`colour '${name}': reset must be keep or restore, not '${d.reset}'`);
        }
      }
      return {
        defaults,
        keepOnReset: COLOURS.filter(c => keep.has(c)),
        warnings,
      };
    }

The text of a tokens element: nothing at all means one token, a number is that
many, and anything else counts as one since the element is there.

    function countFromText(text: string): number {
      const n = parseInt(text.trim(), 10);
      return Number.isNaN(n) ? 1 : Math.max(0, n);
    }

    function exportPNML(gn: GameNet, netName: string): string {
      const { net } = gn;
      const lines: string[] = [];

      lines.push('<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>');
      lines.push('<pnml xmlns="http://www.pnml.org/version-2009/grammar/pnml">');
      lines.push(`  <net id="pn-chomper" type="http://www.pnml.org/version-2009/grammar/ptnet">`);
      lines.push(`    <name><text>${escXml(netName)}</text></name>`);

      // Net-level toolspecific
      lines.push('    <toolspecific tool="pn-chomper" version="1.0">');
      const keep = gn.keepOnReset ?? DEFAULT_KEEP;
      if (keep.join() !== DEFAULT_KEEP.join()) {
        // Only a map that differs from the built-ins needs to say so.
        const reset = (c: ColourName) => keep.includes(c) ? 'keep' : 'restore';
        lines.push('      <colours>');
        lines.push(`        <colour name="chomper" marking="initial" reset="${reset('chomper')}"/>`);
        lines.push(`        <colour name="ghost" reset="${reset('ghost')}"/>`);
        lines.push(`        <colour name="dot" reset="${reset('dot')}"/>`);
        lines.push('      </colours>');
      }
      if (gn.nodeRadius !== undefined) {
        lines.push(`      <nodeRadius>${gn.nodeRadius}</nodeRadius>`);
      }
      lines.push('    </toolspecific>');

      lines.push('    <page id="page1">');

      // Places
      for (const p of net.places.values()) {
        lines.push(`      <place id="${escXml(p.id)}">`);
        lines.push(`        <name><text>${escXml(p.label)}</text></name>`);
        lines.push(`        <graphics><position x="${p.x}" y="${p.y}"/></graphics>`);
        const marking = tokenCount(gn.chomperStart, p.id);
        lines.push(`        <initialMarking><text>${marking}</text></initialMarking>`);
        lines.push('        <toolspecific tool="pn-chomper" version="1.0">');
        if (marking > 0) lines.push('          <playerStart/>');
        // A colour's built-in default is none for ghosts and one for dots,
        // so only a count that differs from that is written.
        const ghosts = tokenCount(gn.ghostStart, p.id);
        if (ghosts > 0)    lines.push(`          <tokens colour="ghost">${ghosts}</tokens>`);
        const dots = tokenCount(gn.dotStart, p.id);
        if (dots !== 1)    lines.push(`          <tokens colour="dot">${dots}</tokens>`);
        lines.push('        </toolspecific>');
        lines.push('      </place>');
      }

      // Transitions
      for (const t of net.transitions.values()) {
        lines.push(`      <transition id="${escXml(t.id)}">`);
        lines.push(`        <name><text>${escXml(t.label)}</text></name>`);
        lines.push(`        <graphics><position x="${t.x}" y="${t.y}"/></graphics>`);
        lines.push('      </transition>');
      }

      // Arcs
      for (const arc of net.arcs) {
        lines.push(`      <arc id="${escXml(arc.id)}" source="${escXml(arc.source)}" target="${escXml(arc.target)}">`);
        lines.push(`        <inscription><text>${arc.weight}</text></inscription>`);
        lines.push('      </arc>');
      }

      lines.push('    </page>');
      lines.push('  </net>');
      lines.push('</pnml>');

      return lines.join('\n');
    }

    function escXml(s: string): string {
      return s.replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
              .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
              .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
              .replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
    }

    type RawPlace = {
      id: string; label: string; x: number; y: number;
      dots: number; isStart: boolean; marking: number;
      ghostStart?: number;    // ghosts that begin here; absent or 0 for none
    };
    type RawTrans = { id: string; label: string; x: number; y: number };
    type RawArc   = { id: string; src: string; tgt: string; weight: number };

    function buildGameNet(
      rawPlaces: RawPlace[],
      rawTrans:  RawTrans[],
      rawArcs:   RawArc[],
      nodeRadius?: number,
      keepOnReset?: ColourName[],
    ): GameNet {
      const allX = [...rawPlaces, ...rawTrans].map(n => n.x);
      const allY = [...rawPlaces, ...rawTrans].map(n => n.y);
      const minX = Math.min(...allX), maxX = Math.max(...allX);
      const minY = Math.min(...allY), maxY = Math.max(...allY);
      const PAD = 80, CW = 950, CH = 780;
      const sc  = Math.min(
        (maxX > minX) ? (CW - 2 * PAD) / (maxX - minX) : 1,
        (maxY > minY) ? (CH - 2 * PAD) / (maxY - minY) : 1,
      );
      const fx = (x: number) => (x - minX) * sc + PAD;
      const fy = (y: number) => (y - minY) * sc + PAD;

      const net = makeNet();
      for (const p of rawPlaces) {
        const gp = addPlace(net, p.id, p.label, fx(p.x), fy(p.y)) as GamePlace;
        gp.dots = p.dots;
      }
      for (const t of rawTrans) {
        addTransition(net, t.id, t.label, fx(t.x), fy(t.y));
      }
      for (const arc of rawArcs) {
        try { addArc(net, arc.id, arc.src, arc.tgt, arc.weight); } catch { /* skip malformed arcs */ }
      }

      type StartEntry = { id: string; count: number };
      let startEntries: StartEntry[];
      const isStartPlaces = rawPlaces.filter(p => p.isStart);
      if (isStartPlaces.length > 0) {
        startEntries = isStartPlaces.map(p => ({ id: p.id, count: p.marking > 0 ? p.marking : 1 }));
      } else {
        const withTokens = rawPlaces.filter(p => p.marking > 0);
        if (withTokens.length > 0) {
          startEntries = withTokens.map(p => ({ id: p.id, count: p.marking }));
        } else {
          startEntries = rawPlaces[0] ? [{ id: rawPlaces[0].id, count: 1 }] : [];
        }
      }
      const chomperStart = emptyMarking();
      for (const e of startEntries) markingAddTokens(chomperStart, e.id, e.count);

      const ghostStart = emptyMarking();
      for (const p of rawPlaces) {
        if ((p.ghostStart ?? 0) > 0) markingAddTokens(ghostStart, p.id, p.ghostStart!);
      }

      const dotStart = dotsOf(net);

      return {
        net, chomperStart, ghostStart, dotStart,
        ...(keepOnReset !== undefined ? { keepOnReset } : {}),
        ...(nodeRadius !== undefined ? { nodeRadius } : {}),
      };
    }

How many tokens of a colour a place's toolspecific block gives it: the count
in the tokens element for that colour if there is one, and the colour's
default if there is not.

    function colourCount(
      ts: Element | null, colour: ColourName, dflt: number,
    ): number {
      if (!ts) return dflt;
      for (const el of ts.querySelectorAll('tokens')) {
        if (el.getAttribute('colour') === colour)
          return countFromText(el.textContent ?? '');
      }
      return dflt;
    }

    function numberAttr(el: Element, name: string): number | undefined {
      const v = el.getAttribute(name);
      return v === null ? undefined : parseInt(v, 10);
    }

    function importPNML(xmlString: string): GameNet {
      const doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(xmlString, 'application/xml');
      if (doc.querySelector('parsererror'))
        throw new Error('PNML parse error');

      function nodeText(el: Element, sel: string): string {
        return el.querySelector(sel)?.textContent?.trim() ?? '';
      }
      function nodePos(el: Element): { x: number; y: number } {
        const p = el.querySelector('graphics > position');
        return { x: parseFloat(p?.getAttribute('x') ?? '0'), y: parseFloat(p?.getAttribute('y') ?? '0') };
      }

      const declared: RawColour[] = [];
      for (const el of doc.querySelectorAll(
        'net > toolspecific[tool="pn-chomper"] > colours > colour',
      )) {
        declared.push({
          name:    el.getAttribute('name') ?? '',
          default: numberAttr(el, 'default'),
          marking: el.getAttribute('marking') ?? undefined,
          reset:   el.getAttribute('reset') ?? undefined,
        });
      }
      const rules = resolveColours(declared);
      for (const w of rules.warnings) console.warn('PNML:', w);

      const rawPlaces: RawPlace[] = [];
      for (const el of doc.querySelectorAll('place')) {
        const id = el.getAttribute('id') ?? '';
        const ts = el.querySelector('toolspecific[tool="pn-chomper"]');
        rawPlaces.push({
          id, label: nodeText(el, 'name > text') || id,
          ...nodePos(el),
          dots:    colourCount(ts, 'dot', rules.defaults.dot),
          isStart: !!ts?.querySelector('playerStart'),
          marking: parseInt(nodeText(el, 'initialMarking > text') || '0', 10),
          ghostStart: colourCount(ts, 'ghost', rules.defaults.ghost),
        });
      }

      const rawTrans: RawTrans[] = [];
      for (const el of doc.querySelectorAll('transition')) {
        const id = el.getAttribute('id') ?? '';
        rawTrans.push({
          id, label: nodeText(el, 'name > text') || id,
          ...nodePos(el),
        });
      }

      const rawArcs: RawArc[] = [];
      for (const el of doc.querySelectorAll('arc')) {
        rawArcs.push({
          id:     el.getAttribute('id') ?? '',
          src:    el.getAttribute('source') ?? '',
          tgt:    el.getAttribute('target') ?? '',
          weight: parseInt(el.querySelector('inscription > text')?.textContent?.trim() ?? '1', 10),
        });
      }

      const nrText = doc.querySelector('net > toolspecific[tool="pn-chomper"] > nodeRadius')
                       ?.textContent?.trim();
      const nodeRadius = nrText ? parseInt(nrText, 10) : undefined;

      // Only a map that differs from the built-ins carries a keepOnReset.
      const keep = rules.keepOnReset.join() === DEFAULT_KEEP.join()
        ? undefined : rules.keepOnReset;

      return buildGameNet(rawPlaces, rawTrans, rawArcs, nodeRadius, keep);
    }

    function downloadPNML(gn: GameNet, name: string): void {
      const xml  = exportPNML(gn, name);
      const blob = new Blob([xml], { type: 'application/xml' });
      const url  = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      const a    = document.createElement('a');
      a.href     = url;
      a.download = name.replace(/[^a-z0-9]/gi, '_').toLowerCase() + '.pnml';
      a.click();
      URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
    }

The buildGameNet examples below use hand-constructed raw records to verify
assembly without a browser.

    const _rp1: RawPlace = { id: 'a', label: 'A', x: 0,   y: 0, dots: 1, isStart: true,  marking: 0 };
    const _rp2: RawPlace = {
      id: 'b', label: 'B', x: 100, y: 0, dots: 3, isStart: false,
      marking: 0, ghostStart: 2,
    };
    const _rt1: RawTrans = { id: 't', label: 'T', x: 50,  y: 0 };
    const _ra1: RawArc   = { id: 'arc1', src: 'a', tgt: 't', weight: 1 };
    const _builtGn = buildGameNet([_rp1, _rp2], [_rt1], [_ra1]);

~example
    tokenCount(_builtGn.chomperStart, 'a') === 1
    tokenCount(_builtGn.chomperStart, 'b') === 0
    tokenCount(_builtGn.ghostStart, 'b') === 2
    tokenCount(_builtGn.ghostStart, 'a') === 0
    _builtGn.net.places.has('a')
    _builtGn.net.places.has('b')
    tokenCount(_builtGn.dotStart, 'a') === 1
    tokenCount(_builtGn.dotStart, 'b') === 3
    _builtGn.net.arcs.length === 1

~property chomperStart_from_isStart
    fc.assert(fc.property(
      fc.integer({ min: 0, max: 5 }),
      fc.integer({ min: 1, max: 5 }),
      (startIdx, total) => {
        const places: RawPlace[] = Array.from({ length: total }, (_, i) => ({
          id: `p${i}`, label: `P${i}`, x: i * 10, y: 0,
          dots: 1, isStart: i === startIdx % total, marking: 0,
        }));
        const gn = buildGameNet(places, [], []);
        return tokenCount(gn.chomperStart, `p${startIdx % total}`) === 1;
      }
    ))

~property all_isStart_in_chomperStart
    fc.assert(fc.property(
      fc.array(fc.boolean(), { minLength: 1, maxLength: 10 }),
      (isStartFlags) => {
        const places: RawPlace[] = isStartFlags.map((isStart, i) => ({
          id: `p${i}`, label: `P${i}`, x: i * 10, y: 0,
          dots: 1, isStart, marking: 0,
        }));
        const gn = buildGameNet(places, [], []);
        const expected = places.filter(p => p.isStart).map(p => p.id);
        return expected.length === 0 ||
          expected.every(id => tokenCount(gn.chomperStart, id) > 0);
      }
    ))

~property scale_fit_positions_within_canvas
    fc.assert(fc.property(
      fc.array(fc.record({ x: fc.integer({ min: -1000, max: 1000 }), y: fc.integer({ min: -1000, max: 1000 }) }), { minLength: 2, maxLength: 10 }),
      (coords) => {
        const places: RawPlace[] = coords.map((c, i) => ({
          id: `p${i}`, label: `P${i}`, x: c.x, y: c.y,
          dots: 1, isStart: i === 0, marking: 0,
        }));
        const gn = buildGameNet(places, [], []);
        const PAD = 80, CW = 950, CH = 780, EPS = 1e-9;
        return [...gn.net.places.values()].every(p =>
          p.x >= PAD - EPS && p.x <= CW - PAD + EPS &&
          p.y >= PAD - EPS && p.y <= CH - PAD + EPS
        );
      }
    ))

~property place_ids_preserved
    fc.assert(fc.property(
      fc.integer({ min: 1, max: 20 }),
      (n) => {
        const places: RawPlace[] = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => ({
          id: `p${i}`, label: `P${i}`, x: i * 10, y: 0,
          dots: 1, isStart: i === 0, marking: 0,
        }));
        const gn = buildGameNet(places, [], []);
        return places.every(p => gn.net.places.has(p.id));
      }
    ))

~property dotStart_marking_matches_raw_counts
    fc.assert(fc.property(
      fc.array(fc.integer({ min: 0, max: 4 }), { minLength: 1, maxLength: 10 }),
      (counts) => {
        const places: RawPlace[] = counts.map((dots, i) => ({
          id: `p${i}`, label: `P${i}`, x: i * 10, y: 0,
          dots, isStart: i === 0, marking: 0,
        }));
        const gn = buildGameNet(places, [], []);
        return counts.every((n, i) => tokenCount(gn.dotStart, `p${i}`) === n);
      }
    ))

~property ghostStart_marking_matches_raw_counts
    fc.assert(fc.property(
      fc.array(fc.integer({ min: 0, max: 4 }), { minLength: 1, maxLength: 10 }),
      (counts) => {
        const places: RawPlace[] = counts.map((ghostStart, i) => ({
          id: `p${i}`, label: `P${i}`, x: i * 10, y: 0,
          dots: 1, isStart: i === 0, marking: 0, ghostStart,
        }));
        const gn = buildGameNet(places, [], []);
        return counts.every((n, i) => tokenCount(gn.ghostStart, `p${i}`) === n);
      }
    ))

What a file says about each place must agree with the map it was written from.
For every built-in map, the chomper, ghost and dot counts a place's block
carries (the initialMarking, the ghost tokens element if there is one, and
the dot tokens element, which means one dot when it is absent) are the counts
in the map's three start markings:

    function _placeBlock(xml: string, id: string): string {
      const start = xml.indexOf(`<place id="${id}">`);
      return xml.slice(start, xml.indexOf('</place>', start));
    }

    function _countIn(block: string, colour: string, absent: number): number {
      const m = block.match(new RegExp(`<tokens colour="${colour}">(\\d+)</tokens>`));
      return m ? parseInt(m[1], 10) : absent;
    }

~property export_agrees_with_the_start_markings
    fc.assert(fc.property(
      fc.constantFrom(
        makeClassicMap, makeSplitMap, makeDiamondMap,
        makeCircuitMap, makeMandalaMap, makeGridMap,
      ),
      (make) => {
        const gn = make();
        const xml = exportPNML(gn, 'agree');
        return [...gn.net.places.keys()].every(id => {
          const block = _placeBlock(xml, id);
          const chomper = parseInt(
            (block.match(/<initialMarking><text>(\d+)<\/text>/) ?? [])[1] ?? '0', 10);
          return chomper === tokenCount(gn.chomperStart, id) &&
                 _countIn(block, 'ghost', 0) === tokenCount(gn.ghostStart, id) &&
                 _countIn(block, 'dot', 1) === tokenCount(gn.dotStart, id);
        });
      }
    ))

~example
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('<pnml')
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('playerStart')
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('<tokens colour="ghost">1</tokens>')
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('<arc ')

~example
    exportPNML(makeGridMap(), 'Grid').includes('<nodeRadius>12</nodeRadius>')
    exportPNML(makeGridMap(), 'Grid').includes('<tokens colour="dot">0</tokens>')
    exportPNML(_builtGn, 'Dots').includes('<tokens colour="dot">3</tokens>')

The declared colours are resolved by a function that needs no DOM, so what a
declaration may and may not change is claimed here. A colour left out of the
declarations keeps its built-in rule.

    const _noDecl      = resolveColours([]);
    const _dotNone     = resolveColours([{ name: 'dot', default: 0 }]);
    const _dotRestore  = resolveColours([{ name: 'dot', reset: 'restore' }]);
    const _ghostKeep   = resolveColours([{ name: 'ghost', reset: 'keep' }]);
    const _unknown     = resolveColours([{ name: 'power', default: 0, reset: 'keep' }]);
    const _chomperOdd  = resolveColours([
      { name: 'chomper', default: 2, marking: 'initial' },
      { name: 'chomper', marking: 'tokens' },
    ]);

~example
    _noDecl.defaults.dot === 1
    _noDecl.defaults.ghost === 0
    _noDecl.defaults.chomper === 0
    _noDecl.keepOnReset.join() === 'dot'
    _noDecl.warnings.length === 0
    _dotNone.defaults.dot === 0
    _dotNone.keepOnReset.join() === 'dot'
    _dotRestore.keepOnReset.length === 0
    _ghostKeep.keepOnReset.join() === 'ghost,dot'
    _unknown.warnings.length === 1
    _unknown.keepOnReset.join() === 'dot'
    _chomperOdd.defaults.chomper === 0
    _chomperOdd.warnings.length === 2
    countFromText('') === 1
    countFromText(' 3 ') === 3
    countFromText('0') === 0
    countFromText('lots') === 1

A map that differs from the built-ins in what it keeps on reset says so in its
declarations, and one that does not says nothing, so an ordinary export has no
header to read past.

    const _keepNone: GameNet = { ...makeCircuitMap(), keepOnReset: [] };

~example
    exportPNML(_keepNone, 'Keep').includes('<colour name="dot" reset="restore"/>')
    !exportPNML(makeCircuitMap(), 'Plain').includes('<colours>')

---

#Tests

##export produces valid XML structure
    exportPNML(makeClassicMap(), 'Classic').includes('<?xml version="1.0"')
    exportPNML(makeClassicMap(), 'Classic').includes('</pnml>')

##every place and transition appears in the export
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('id="start"')
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('id="t_fork"')
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('id="b1"')

##playerStart gets initialMarking 1, others get 0
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('<initialMarking><text>1</text></initialMarking>')

##a ghost's place carries a tokens element, and no transition a spawn mark
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('<tokens colour="ghost">1</tokens>')
    !exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('ghostSpawn')
    !exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('ghostStart')

##a place with several ghosts exports its count
    exportPNML(_builtGn, 'Two').includes('<tokens colour="ghost">2</tokens>')

##a place with its default dot says nothing about it
    !exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('<tokens colour="dot">1</tokens>')

##playerStart place is marked
    exportPNML(makeSplitMap(), 'Split').includes('<playerStart/>')

##nodeRadius appears when set
    exportPNML(makeGridMap(), 'Grid').includes('<nodeRadius>12</nodeRadius>')

##nodeRadius absent when not set
    !exportPNML(makeClassicMap(), 'Classic').includes('<nodeRadius>')

##special XML characters are escaped
    escXml('a & b < c > d "e"') === 'a &amp; b &lt; c &gt; d &quot;e&quot;'


